# Portable runtime state
telegram-mcp-server/.env.local
telegram-mcp-server/queue.db
# Scratch outputs. Root-anchored: an unanchored name would match vault/Tmp, vault/Dist,
# vault/Logs and vault/Projects on a case-insensitive filesystem.
/tmp/
/dist/
coverage/
node_modules/
# Relay daemon runtime scratch (inbox, logs) lives only at the hub root; an
# unanchored rule would also swallow the shipped pipelines/deploy/relay/ module.
# memory-index CLI local index — regenerated via `npm run memory-index -- build`
.memory-index.json
dev-server.log
# Tip rotation memory written by lib/tips.js
# Agent run records written by `npm run task -- run` on hubs without a vault
# (a vault hub keeps them under vault/Workspace/Runs, already ignored above)
/.agent-runs/
# dep-graph MCP baseline() output, written next to the scanned directory
workspace-identity.mdc
copilot-instructions.md
# Generated by deploy (hooks, MCP, permissions); regenerated on every deploy and
# accumulates local permissions.allow entries, so it differs per clone
.env
# Setup-owned: created from the shipped pipelines/deploy/templates/hub-mcp.json, then
# gains the machine-specific qmd entry. Anchored so the template stays tracked.
/.mcp.json
# Obsidian per-user state: everything under vault/.obsidian/ stays out of git. That
# covers every plugin's data.json (the REST API plugin's holds the API key, a
# certificate and its private key), user-installed plugins, workspace.json, graph.json
# and the plugin config files. Setup recreates the two plugin config files from
# templates/vault-plugin-config/ and downloads the code of the three shipped plugins
# (lib/vault-plugin-install.js), so a plugin that Obsidian upgrades never dirties the tree.
# User content in the vault. A release tracks only its shipped notes (vault/Agistra,
# vault/Templates and the _welcome.md of Memory and Workspace); everything a user or a
# tool writes there stays out of git status. Contents-plus-negation: a directory that is
# itself ignored cannot be re-included. Root-anchored, so a project folder or a note
# named like these elsewhere is unaffected.
# Generated by lib/vault-index.js: vault/vault-index.md and one <category>-index.md in
# each top-level vault folder (agistra-index.md, templates-index.md, ...).
# Installed third-party skills and agents (install-skill, setup). Skill bodies live in
# skills/third-party/, subagent definitions in <adapter>/agents/third-party/.
/logs/
# Free-tier learnings store: local session state, like memory/
.learnings/
/memory/
/projects/
.graphify/
package-lock.json
# Package-owned runtime manifests: setup runs npm ci --prefix against these locks
!/packages/obsidian-mcp-server/package-lock.json
!/packages/qmd/package-lock.json
graphify-out/
